          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Packet handlers run before CONNECT, bypassing authentication and dereferencing a NULL session\n\nprocess_message dispatches every decoded packet without checking client->connected or that a session exists. Authentication happens only inside connect_handler, so with allow_anonymous=false an unauthenticated client can still send PUBLISH (including RETAIN) and inject messages into broker topics. Session-dependent packets such as SUBSCRIBE, PUBACK, PUBREC and PUBCOMP similarly run with client->session == NULL and crash the broker.\n\nSeverity: high\n\nCategory: Access control\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-306, CWE-287, CWE-476\n\nRemediation:\nReject every packet other than CONNECT until the connection has completed a successful CONNECT and has a non-NULL session. Enforce authorization in the dispatch layer, not only in connect_handler, and return a protocol error for premature packets.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- With allow_anonymous=false, send PUBLISH as the first packet and assert the broker rejects it and does not store a retained message.\n- Send SUBSCRIBE, PUBACK, PUBREC and PUBCOMP before CONNECT; assert each is rejected without a crash.\n- Add a state-machine test that only CONNECT is accepted in the initial state.\n\nPreventive controls:\n- Add an explicit connection state machine and authorize at dispatch time.\n- Treat any non-CONNECT packet received before CONNECT as a protocol violation and close the connection."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:a35fde2686bd3da677426585f68f6c3ec235cf6fa2a1950b97a033545931a853"
