          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "UNSUBSCRIBE packet is destroyed twice, causing a heap double free\n\nunsubscribe_handler calls mqtt_packet_destroy(&e->data) before returning REPLY, and process_message then calls mqtt_packet_destroy(&io.data) again for every non-PUBLISH reply. The destructor frees the topic tuples without clearing the pointers, so a pre-CONNECT UNSUBSCRIBE triggers a double free of the tuple array and each topic string.\n\nSeverity: high\n\nCategory: Memory corruption\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-415, CWE-416\n\nRemediation:\nRemove the mqtt_packet_destroy call from unsubscribe_handler and let process_message own packet destruction, or transfer ownership explicitly. Make the destructor idempotent by clearing pointers and lengths after freeing.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Send UNSUBSCRIBE with one topic on a fresh connection under ASan; assert no double-free report.\n- Add a test that verifies process_message is the sole owner of decoded packet destruction.\n\nPreventive controls:\n- Define one owner for each decoded packet and document the ownership transfer at the handler boundary.\n- Null out freed pointers in mqtt_packet_destroy to make repeated destruction harmless."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:a36abc76b24396d7a5508ccf4d3acd0071b2c403844f29569bfeac946b822122"
          },
