          "message": {
            "text": "Packet type dispatch tables contain NULL and out-of-bounds entries\n\nmqtt_unpack indexes unpack_handlers[byte >> 4] and handle_command indexes handlers[type] without checking that the type is implemented. CONNACK (0x20), SUBACK (0x90) and the unmapped types 0xB0/0xD0 survive the opcode range check and reach a NULL function pointer or an out-of-bounds table read, crashing the single-process broker before authentication.\n\nSeverity: high\n\nCategory: Denial of service\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-476, CWE-129\n\nRemediation:\nValidate the packet type before both dispatch tables, reject every type the broker does not implement, and size the tables to the full 0-15 range with explicit NULL checks. Return a protocol error instead of calling through a missing entry.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Send 0x20 0x00, 0x90 0x00, 0xB0 0x00 and 0xD0 0x00 to a fresh connection; assert each is rejected with a protocol error and the broker remains alive.\n- Fuzz all 256 first bytes with a zero remaining length under ASan/UBSan.\n\nPreventive controls:\n- Guard both dispatch sites with a range check and a non-NULL check.\n- Use a single table sized 16 with explicit handlers for every defined type and reject the rest."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:254634f01c141bce779fe5fdd3c9be274baff833465395cf3e19bf16ecf915c5"
          },
          "properties": {
