            {
              "message": {
                "text": "evidence:takeover-duplicate-map-entry"
              },
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/handlers.c"
                },
                "region": {
                  "endLine": 425,
                  "startLine": 424
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Duplicate client IDs share a session and free it while another connection still uses it\n\nconnect_handler looks up an existing session by client ID and reuses it for the new connection without disconnecting the old client or removing its clients_map entry. If the new connection keeps clean_session=false, both connections point at the same session; when the original connection later disconnects with clean_session=true, client_deactivate frees that session while the new connection still references it. Duplicate HASH_ADD_STR entries and the HASH_DEL of a shared session worsen the corruption.\n\nSeverity: high\n\nCategory: Memory corruption\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-416, CWE-362\n\nRemediation:\nOn a duplicate client ID, disconnect and unregister the existing connection before adopting its session (MQTT takeover semantics), or reject the new connection. Keep exactly one clients_map entry per client ID and reference-count sessions by owning connection.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Open two connections with the same client ID and clean_session=false, then disconnect the first with clean_session=true and publish/subscribe from the second under ASan.\n- Assert the broker keeps exactly one clients_map entry per client ID after a takeover.\n- Add a takeover test that verifies the old connection is closed before the new connection adopts the session.\n\nPreventive controls:\n- Implement MQTT 3.1.1 session takeover by closing the existing connection and removing its map entry before reusing the session.\n- Reference-count sessions by connection and free them only when the last owner releases them."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:36190936656c60bfc5bdde3986e862b8bf82eecc7332e6135cd8b9b7f9395740"
          },
