          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Pre-authenticated CONNECT client ID overflows a 64-byte field on the stack\n\nunpack_mqtt_connect reads an attacker-controlled 16-bit client ID length and copies that many bytes into connect.payload.client_id, a 64-byte array, then writes a NUL at client_id[cid_len]. The decoded packet lives in the stack-local io_event of process_message, so a CONNECT whose client ID exceeds 63 bytes overwrites the process_message stack frame with attacker bytes before any authentication.\n\nSeverity: critical\n\nCategory: Memory corruption\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-121, CWE-787\n\nRemediation:\nReject CONNECT when cid_len >= MQTT_CLIENT_ID_LEN or when cid_len exceeds the remaining packet body, and copy with a bounded length. Prefer allocating client IDs dynamically or enforcing the MQTT 3.1.1 23-byte minimum limit.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Send a CONNECT with a 64-byte client ID; assert it is rejected without corruption.\n- Send a CONNECT with a 4096-byte client ID; assert the broker rejects it and stays alive (ASan build).\n- Fuzz cid_len against lengths just under and over the 64-byte boundary.\n\nPreventive controls:\n- Validate every attacker-supplied length against both the remaining packet size and the destination capacity before copying.\n- Keep decoded packet storage off the stack or use dynamically sized fields."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:626b7c313a2050966b0acc616a93d4eb510b4c1588c3a21e98f85cf4197fb1d2"
          },
