            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Inflight ACK retransmission packs through a NULL packet pointer\n\ninflight_msg_check resends pending ACKs with mqtt_pack(p, c->wbuf + c->towrite), but p is only assigned in the preceding message branch and is NULL when only an ACK is pending. A client can create an ACK-only inflight entry by sending PUBREC for an unused packet ID; after the 20-second retransmission timer, mqtt_pack dereferences NULL and crashes the broker. The call also uses the wrong buffer size, since size was computed from the ACK packet.\n\nSeverity: medium\n\nCategory: Denial of service\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-476\n\nRemediation:\nPass &ack to mqtt_pack in the ACK branch and compute the size from the same packet that is serialized. Reset p per iteration or avoid sharing it between the two branches.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Send PUBREC with an unused packet ID from a connected client, wait for the timer, and assert no crash.\n- Unit-test inflight_msg_check with an ACK-only session entry.\n\nPreventive controls:\n- Serialize the packet that was built in the same branch and scope the retransmission pointer to each branch.\n- Validate packet identifiers before storing ACK state."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
