          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Unsigned remaining-length arithmetic underflows in the MQTT decoder\n\nunpack_mqtt_publish, unpack_mqtt_subscribe and unpack_mqtt_unsubscribe subtract header, topic and QoS lengths from the usize remaining length without checking that each field fits. A PUBLISH whose remaining length is smaller than 2 + topiclen wraps len to a huge value, and unpack_bytes then allocates len + 1 and memcpy's len bytes from the packet buffer. SUBSCRIBE/UNSUBSCRIBE loops similarly wrap and keep allocating and reading past the packet.\n\nSeverity: high\n\nCategory: Memory safety\n\nWeaknesses: CWE-191, CWE-125, CWE-787\n\nRemediation:\nBefore each subtraction, verify that the field length fits in the remaining bytes (remaining >= 1 + 2 + topic_len for SUBSCRIBE tuples, and remaining >= 2 + topic_len for PUBLISH). Reject truncated packets with a protocol error instead of subtracting.\n\nRemediation tests:\n- Send PUBLISH packets with remaining lengths 0-4 and topic length 0 under ASan; assert a clean protocol error.\n- Send SUBSCRIBE and UNSUBSCRIBE packets with a single trailing byte; assert the decoder terminates with an error.\n- Fuzz remaining length, topic length and tuple count combinations under ASan/UBSan.\n\nPreventive controls:\n- Use checked subtraction helpers that return an error when the field does not fit in the remaining bytes.\n- Bound every decoder allocation by the received packet size."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:f34bb683986e78a0569fc1f6a6eb75a9e17e08e7450010055cc6501e4ce1498c"
          },
          "properties": {
            "category": "memory-safety",
            "confidence": "high",
            "findingId": "csf_0e8e471e474aae0c70a637ff",
            "occurrenceId": "occ_eb3368c883ea7c72daeb5eda",
            "severity": "high"
          },
          "ruleId": "memory-safety.decoder-length-underflow",
          "ruleIndex": 3
        }
      ],
