            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Memory safety: Session takeover use after free. Categories: Memory corruption. Weaknesses: CWE-362, CWE-416."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Memory safety: Session takeover use after free. Categories: Memory corruption. Weaknesses: CWE-362, CWE-416.\n\n## Remediation\n\nOn a duplicate client ID, disconnect and unregister the existing connection before adopting its session (MQTT takeover semantics), or reject the new connection. Keep exactly one clients_map entry per client ID and reference-count sessions by owning connection.",
                "text": "Memory safety: Session takeover use after free. Categories: Memory corruption. Weaknesses: CWE-362, CWE-416.\n\nRemediation:\n\nOn a duplicate client ID, disconnect and unregister the existing connection before adopting its session (MQTT takeover semantics), or reject the new connection. Keep exactly one clients_map entry per client ID and reference-count sessions by owning connection."
              },
              "id": "memory-safety.session-takeover-use-after-free",
              "name": "Memory safety: Session takeover use after free",
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "8.1",
                "tags": [
                  "external/cwe/cwe-362",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-416",
                  "memory-corruption",
                  "security"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Memory safety: Session takeover use after free"
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Memory safety: Unsubscribe double free. Categories: Memory corruption. Weaknesses: CWE-415, CWE-416."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Memory safety: Unsubscribe double free. Categories: Memory corruption. Weaknesses: CWE-415, CWE-416.\n\n## Remediation\n\nRemove the mqtt_packet_destroy call from unsubscribe_handler and let process_message own packet destruction, or transfer ownership explicitly. Make the destructor idempotent by clearing pointers and lengths after freeing.",
                "text": "Memory safety: Unsubscribe double free. Categories: Memory corruption. Weaknesses: CWE-415, CWE-416.\n\nRemediation:\n\nRemove the mqtt_packet_destroy call from unsubscribe_handler and let process_message own packet destruction, or transfer ownership explicitly. Make the destructor idempotent by clearing pointers and lengths after freeing."
              },
              "id": "memory-safety.unsubscribe-double-free",
              "name": "Memory safety: Unsubscribe double free",
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "8.1",
